<statement>
<p>
Solve the following linear system.  If the system has an infinite number of solutions, parameterize the solution set in terms of the free variables of the original system.</p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{\left\lbrace\begin{array}{ccccccccccc} -{3}{x}\amp-\amp{9}{y}\amp+\amp{5}{z}\amp-\amp{34}{w}\amp+\amp{25}{v}\amp=\amp-{60}\\-{4}{x}\amp-\amp{12}{y}\amp-\amp{5}{z}\amp-\amp{22}{w}\amp-\amp{60}{v}\amp=\amp{25}\\-{6}{x}\amp-\amp{18}{y}\amp+\amp{6}{z}\amp-\amp{60}{w}\amp+\amp{18}{v}\amp=\amp-{84}\end{array}\right.}</m></p>
<p>
x = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
y = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
z = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
w = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
v = <fillin characters="20"/>  

</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li><m>\displaystyle{5}-{3}{y}-{8}{w}-{5}{v}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{y}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle-{9}+{2}{w}-{8}{v}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{w}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{v}</m></li></ul></p>
</answer>

